---
import Base from '../../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import NnMasthead from '../../../../components/NnMasthead.astro';
import race from '../../../../content/race.json';

import '@src/shared/styles/nn-theme.css';

/**
 * Where Stripe sends somebody after the payment page.
 *
 * ## The rule this page is built on
 *
 * **Only "paid" makes a positive claim, and no state ever makes a negative one.**
 *
 * The first half is obvious. The second half is the one that matters, and it is why this page
 * no longer says "nothing has been charged" anywhere. The sequence it prevents: somebody pays,
 * the webhook is delayed or lost, their thirty-one minute hold lapses, they refresh this page.
 * If it then tells them nothing was charged, they go back to `/nn/` and pay again — and the
 * club has taken £34 from somebody who wanted one race, and hears about it from them rather
 * than from the system.
 *
 * So the blocks below say what the club has **recorded**, never what the bank did.
 *
 * ## Arriving here is still not proof of payment
 *
 *   1. The redirect fires in the person's browser. A closed tab means it never fires, while
 *      the payment may still have gone through.
 *   2. It is an ordinary URL. Anybody can type it, and the acceptance suite does exactly that
 *      with a session id that matches nothing.
 *   3. Stripe confirms to the **webhook**, server to server — the only channel that cannot be
 *      forged or lost in a tab.
 *
 * What changed in this slice is that the webhook exists, so there is a recorded fact to
 * report. The page reports that record and never the redirect it arrived by.
 * `entries.entry_completion_state()` returns **one word and nothing else** — not the name, not
 * the email address, not the amount, not the purchase id — because a session id in a URL is
 * not authentication.
 *
 * ## Four blocks, one of which ships visible
 *
 * `data-complete-confirming` is served **visible** and the other three `hidden`; the Worker
 * hides it and reveals one of them. So "still confirming" needs no rewriting to happen, which
 * means the ordinary path and every failure path — migration not landed, database unreachable,
 * no session in the URL — produce byte-identical HTML, and the state that claims least is the
 * one that happens by default.
 *
 * `lapsed` and `unknown` share the "no record" block. To the person reading it they are the
 * same message, and one of the ways `unknown` happens is a purchase whose Checkout session id
 * had not been written back yet — where "we have never heard of this" would be actively wrong.
 *
 * ## There is no auto-refresh, and that is a decision
 *
 * A `<meta http-equiv="refresh">` on the pending state is the obvious thing and it is not
 * allowed here: a delayed refresh under twenty hours fails **WCAG 2.2.1**, axe reports it as
 * `meta-refresh` under `wcag2a`, and zero violations is not a threshold in this repository. It
 * is also hostile in exactly the situation it would be used — a page reloading under somebody
 * who is reading it, on a phone, having just paid. There is no polling script either; this
 * site has no client-side state and does not start here.
 *
 * The pending block carries a plain link to this same address instead. `href=""` is a relative
 * reference that resolves to the current URL **with its query string and without its
 * fragment**, so the link carries the session id without this static page having to know it.
 */

const canonical = 'https://new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk/nn/2026/entry/complete/';
---

<Base
  title="Your Nightingale Nightmare entry"
  description="What the club has recorded about your Nightingale Nightmare entry, and what happens next."
  canonical={canonical}
  theme="nn"
>
  {
    /* **The wordmark without the links, and this is the only page that gets that.**
    Somebody arrives here having just paid, to find out whether the club knows it. Four
    links offering the course, the race-day plan and the spectator guide are four ways to
    leave before reading the one paragraph that answers the question they came with. The
    mark stays so the page is visibly still the club's. */
  }
  <NnMasthead slot="masthead" nav={false} />

  <header class="nn-hero nn-hero-compact">
    <div class="nn-wrap">
      <h1>Your entry</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="nn-wrap">
    {
      /* `role="status"` rather than `alert` on all four: this is the page's subject, arrived
      at by navigation, so it belongs in the ordinary reading order rather than interrupting.
      Only one is ever visible, and each says in words what it is — the colour carries none of
      the meaning. */
    }

    {
      /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Still confirming. **Ships visible**, and is what every failure path leaves on the page.
      No tick and no green: a tick here would say "done", which is the one thing this block
      does not know. --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    }
    <div class="notice nn-card" data-complete-confirming role="status">
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>The club is confirming your payment with Stripe.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        This usually takes a few seconds. <strong
          >This page cannot yet tell you whether the payment went through</strong
        > — it is shown to everybody who comes back from the payment page, and to anybody who
        types this address.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="">Check again</a> in a moment. Nothing is lost by waiting, and you do not need
        to fill the form in again.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Paid. **The only block on this page that makes a positive claim**, and it is made only
      because the webhook — server to server, signed — recorded it. The tick is the mockup's
      and is hidden from assistive technology: the sentence is what should be announced.
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    }
    <div class="notice notice-ok nn-card" data-complete="paid" hidden role="status">
      <span class="nn-tick" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" focusable="false"
          ><path d="M4 12.5 10 18 20 6"></path></svg
        >
      </span>
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>Your payment is confirmed and your place is booked.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        There is nothing else to do now. Confirmation emails are still being set up, so
        you may not receive one — your place is booked either way, and this page is the
        record.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep this page's address if you would like to check again later. What to do on the
        day is on <a href="/nn/2026/race-day/">the race instructions</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      No payment recorded — a lapsed hold, or a session this club has nothing against.

      **This block must never say that nothing was charged.** It does not know that, and the
      case where it would be wrong is the case where somebody pays twice. Every sentence here
      is about the club's records rather than about anybody's bank.
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    }
    <div class="notice notice-bad nn-card" data-complete="no-record" hidden role="status">
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>The club has not recorded a payment against this address.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If your card was charged, do not enter again.</strong> A payment can take a
        little while to reach the club, and entering twice would mean paying twice. Email{
          ' '
        }
        <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a> with the address of this page
        and the race organisers will find it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you did not finish paying, nothing was taken and you are welcome to{' '}
        <a href="/nn/2026/">start again</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Refunded. A statement of fact from the club's own records, in the plain card rather than
      a coloured one — a refund is not an error.
      --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
    }
    <div class="notice nn-card" data-complete="refunded" hidden role="status">
      <p class="lede"><strong>This entry was refunded.</strong></p>
      <p>
        The club's records show the payment for this entry was returned, so there is no
        place held against it. If that is not what you expected, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a> and the race organisers will check
        it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="nn-card nn-prose">
      <h2>If something does not look right</h2>

      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a> and the race organisers
        will check it against the club's records. Please include the address of this page —
        it identifies the payment without you having to send any card details, which the club
        never wants and never holds.
      </p>

      <p>
        What the club does with your details, and how to have them removed, is in{' '}
        <a href="/nn/privacy/">the privacy notice</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    {
      /* **The way back, and the reason it is one link rather than the navigation bar.**

      This page ships `nav={false}` on the masthead, and the argument for that is good: four
      links offering the course, the race-day plan and the spectator guide are four ways to
      leave before reading the one paragraph somebody came here for. It is right *while* that
      paragraph is being read.

      It was wrong afterwards. The page is a **destination** rather than a step — Stripe sends
      people here, the copy above tells them to keep the address and come back to it later,
      and `/account/entries/` links here too — so most arrivals are people for whom the
      question is already answered, and the only things left to click were a wordmark leading
      out of the campaign entirely and one link to the race-day page. #114.

      One link, below the answer rather than above it, keeps both properties. */
    }
    <p class="nn-back">
      <a href="/nn/2026/">Back to Nightingale Nightmare 2026</a>
    </p>

    <footer>
      <p>Southville Running Club.</p>
      <p>
        Questions? <a href={`mailto:${race.contact}`}>{race.contact}</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Base>
